---
title: Discover, unlock, equip
pageSlug: the-loop
mod: spell-codex
section: gameplay
order: 2
---

The loop never really changes. You find a spell, you pay to rank it up, you put it on the bar, you cast it.

**Discover.** Iron’s schools and addons like [Leylines](/mods/leylines) show up as tabs once the server has seen them. Ways in: Codex pages, converting old scrolls, or shift-right-clicking a filled spellbook to pull the spells out (the book stays, empty). Creative-only Iron’s spells stay hidden unless you flip `includeCreativeSpells` in `codex_settings.json`.

**Unlock.** Discovering a spell is not the same as owning every rank. Pick the matching **ink** under the Codex, then hit **+**. If nothing happens, you have the wrong rarity or you cannot pay the XP.

**Equip.** Click an unlocked spell. If it has several tiers, pick one. Drop it on the action bar. Wide books and long school lists scroll. The little inspector on the left fills in when you click a spell: name, school, mana, cooldown, the guide blurb.

**Cast.** Action bar only. The HUD hides until the first spell is on it.

Edit HUD is the button on the Codex. Action bar, mana, and the cast bar drag separately. Each one has a small scale control. You are not stuck with the default pile above the hotbar.

A pack with many schools will look busy. Use the school arrows, and do not panic if the tab you want is off-screen. Scroll the tab strip.
